    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0783" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg771"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7490F/12–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-12T14:00:00+01:00">December 12,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 12—noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11006. ReDept’s 9918, November 25, 6 p.m. and 10264 December 8, 3 p.m.<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d845-f1"/> Department’s views were presented personally by me
                    to Mr. Eden. In order to be able to reply fully Eden is consulting Foreign
                    Office officials who are directly concerned with certain aspects of this matter.
                    I expect soon to be able to telegraph Eden’s reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
